menu "Modbus (board)"

config MB_RS485_MASTER
    bool "RS-485 master"
    default y
    help
        Lets the board drive the RS-485 segment as its Modbus master, for the
        RS-485 rows of the poll table and, with MB_GATEWAY, for the Modbus
        TCP gateway. Without it the board is only ever an RTU slave on
        RS-485; a configuration that says "master" (stored by the other
        firmware) runs as slave.

config MB_GATEWAY
    bool "Modbus TCP to RS-485 gateway"
    depends on MB_RS485_MASTER
    default y
    help
        Forwards Modbus TCP requests for other unit IDs to the devices on the
        RS-485 segment. Without it a stored "gateway" setting is ignored and
        the master serves the poll table only.

config MB_TCP_MASTER
    bool "Poll table rows on the network (Modbus TCP master)"
    default y
    help
        Lets the poll table read devices over Modbus TCP as well as on
        RS-485. Without it network rows are refused and only RS-485 rows are
        read.

config MB_TCP_MASTER_CONNS
    int "Connections kept open to polled network devices"
    depends on MB_TCP_MASTER
    range 1 8
    default 3
    help
        Sockets the poll table keeps open between polls; the application's
        net_budget.h adds them up against CONFIG_LWIP_MAX_SOCKETS.

config MB_TCP_MAX_CONN
    int "Modbus TCP clients served at once"
    range 1 16
    default 8
    help
        Connections the Modbus TCP server (port 502) keeps open at the same
        time. Each holds an lwIP socket; the application's net_budget.h adds
        them up against CONFIG_LWIP_MAX_SOCKETS. A client arriving with every
        slot taken is accepted and closed at once.

config MB_TCP_BACKLOG
    int "Modbus TCP listen backlog"
    range 1 32
    default 16
    help
        Connections lwIP may complete before the server accepts them. They
        hold a TCP PCB each, not a socket.

endmenu
